{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"yogic-soapstone-takin","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nRepresentation drift (a schema/set/surface and a hand-maintained copy diverging) is the dominant sub-mechanism of the product-logic defect category (R2S1). Three mirror classes are already generated/gated (config↔docs via gen_config_reference.py, env-vars↔docs via gen_env_registry.py, library surface via gen_api_surface.py); the terminal-status set was unified by bug e63c; the MCP↔library gap is a sibling story. This task finds what else remains — unknown mirrors are unknown defect sources.\n\n## Approach\n\nSystematic sweep of src/rebar for hand-maintained duplicates of a canonical fact: enumerations duplicated across modules (status-like sets, error-code lists, event-type lists), doc tables restating code constants, schema fragments re-declared, hardcoded path/name lists mirroring a registry. Method: grep/AST passes for duplicate literal sets + cross-reference with schemas and generators; verify each candidate is a genuine mirror (same fact, two masters) not a distinct concept (the e63c audit's claimability-vs-terminal distinction). Deliverable is an inventory with dispositions; fixes land as follow-up tickets, not in this task.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md committed, listing every candidate examined with verdict {genuine mirror / distinct concept / already gated} and file:line evidence.\n- [ ] AC2: every genuine live mirror has a linked ticket (discovered_from this task) proposing generate-or-gate using the existing pattern.\n- [ ] AC3: the inventory states the sweep method (patterns searched) so it is repeatable.\n- [ ] AC4: sibling story's mirror (MCP↔library) is referenced, not re-filed.\n\n## File impact\n\n- reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md (new; committed report)","id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833","parent_id":"87cb-7121-a3b6-4606","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Representation-mirror inventory sweep: find and disposition remaining hand-maintained mirrors"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788311498329604970,"uuid":"cb9c7749-c114-41d8-9c9c-1bed01ff917a"}